{sk==='alps'&&<><div className="alps-top"><p className="eyebrow">VETTED BY</p><img className="alps-logo" src="./brand/alps-logo.png" alt="ALPS" width="1182" height="476"/></div><div className="alps-hero" style={{backgroundImage:'url(./brand/alps-mountains.webp)'}}><h2>Vetted by ALPS for its<br/><em>on-prem agentic capabilities.</em></h2></div><div className="alps-about"><div className="stat"><strong>225<span>+</span></strong><p>ALPS Advisors</p></div><p className="alps-desc">ALPS is an <b>Enterprise Marketplace</b> with experience bringing best-of-class solutions to <b>Fortune 500</b> companies through its network of 225+ ALPS Advisors.</p></div></>}
{sk==='problem'&&<><p className="eyebrow">THE SITUATION</p><h2>A thin margin.<br/><em>An expensive revenue cycle.</em></h2><div className="problem"><div><div className="chart-label">OF EVERY $100 IN NET PATIENT REVENUE</div><div className="split-bar" role="img" aria-label="Of every 100 dollars of net revenue, about 88 dollars cover everything else, 10 dollars run the revenue cycle, and 1 dollar 70 is kept as operating margin"><i className="rest" style={{flex:88.3}}/><i className="rcm" style={{flex:10}}/><i className="kept" style={{flex:1.7}}/></div><div className="split-key"><span><i className="rest"/>$88.30 everything else</span><span><i className="rcm"/>$10 running the revenue cycle</span><span><i className="kept"/>$1.70 kept as operating margin</span></div><p className="problem-note">The median hospital keeps <em>$1.70</em>. Running the revenue cycle costs roughly six times what it keeps.</p></div><div className="reasons"><div><strong>12–13<small>%</small></strong><h3>of claims denied</h3><p>Growing about 20% a year.</p></div><div><strong>+25<small>%</small></strong><h3>cost to collect, year over year</h3><p>Still rising, even with offshoring.</p></div><div><strong>70<small>%</small></strong><h3>of denials never worked</h3><p>Written off rather than reworked.</p></div></div></div><p className="problem-so">More claims get denied, each denial costs more to chase, and less of what is chased ever comes back. <em>Fix one in isolation and the other two absorb the loss.</em></p></>}
