{sk==='reading'&&<><p className="eyebrow">APPENDIX / FURTHER READING</p><h2>Two reads.<br/><em>The same conclusion from the field.</em></h2><div className="reading"><a className="reading-item" href="https://www.ey.com/en_us/insights/health/ai-driven-rcm-in-healthcare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span className="reading-pub">EY · INSIGHTS · 27 MAR 2026</span><h3>How AI can transform the revenue cycle in healthcare</h3><p>Jon Rasul, EY Health Consulting revenue cycle leader, on why denials keep rising and how AI moves the revenue cycle from a back-office cost to a source of value.</p><ul className="reading-facts"><li>Nearly half of provider organizations report 10% or more of their claims denied.</li><li>The share with denial rates of 10% or more rose from 30% in 2022 to 41% in 2025.</li><li>59% plan to invest in claims processing or denial reduction technology within six months.</li></ul><span className="reading-link">Read at ey.com <ExternalLink size={14}/></span></a><a className="reading-item" href="https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/finance/cleveland-clinics-15b-revenue-cycle-and-the-unsustainable-problem-it-hopes-to-solve/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span className="reading-pub">BECKER’S HOSPITAL REVIEW · 25 JUN 2026</span><h3>Cleveland Clinic’s $15B revenue cycle and the ‘unsustainable’ problem it hopes to solve</h3><p>Alan Condon on a $15B revenue cycle that still sees 15% of claims denied, overturns 92% only after rework, and is turning to upstream prevention and AI with a person in the loop.</p><ul className="reading-facts"><li>15% incoming denial rate, 92% overturned, net controllable loss under 2%.</li><li>Two medical directors embedded in revenue cycle operations to prevent denials.</li><li>About 200 automation bots, with a person validating every AI coding result.</li></ul><span className="reading-link">Read at beckershospitalreview.com <ExternalLink size={14}/></span></a></div><p className="fine">Third-party publications, linked for reference. Neither describes a Contiinex engagement. See the case study slide and the source notes for full citations.</p></>}
